{
  "title": "First and Last Lesson per Streak",
  "prompt": "You're analyzing learner engagement in a language learning app. The `streak_lessons` table records every lesson completed during active learning streaks. Each row has a unique `lesson_id`, the learner's `user_id`, the date the lesson was completed (`completion_date`), the `streak_id` identifying which streak the lesson belongs to, and the `lesson_title`. Write a query that returns, for each lesson, the lesson's own details plus the title of the FIRST lesson and the LAST lesson completed in that streak. The output should include: `lesson_id`, `user_id`, `streak_id`, `completion_date`, `lesson_title`, `first_lesson_in_streak` (the title of the earliest lesson in that streak), and `last_lesson_in_streak` (the title of the final lesson in that streak). Order the result by `user_id`, `streak_id`, `completion_date`. Note that some streaks may have only one lesson (so first and last are the same), and ensure your window frame captures the true last value of the partition, not just the current row.",
